{"path":"experimental/dynamic/strdup","title":"strdup","titleHtml":"strdup","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/experimental/dynamic/strdup","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a pointer to a null-terminated byte string, which is a duplicate of the string pointed to by str1. The returned pointer must be passed to free to avoid a memory leak.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte\"><code>&lt;string.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> strdup<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>str1 <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-dynamic-tr t-mark-ts\">(dynamic memory TR)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a pointer to a null-terminated byte string, which is a duplicate\nof the string pointed to by <code>str1</code>. The returned pointer must be passed to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/memory/free\">free</a></span> to avoid a memory leak.\n</p><p>If an error occurs, a null pointer is returned and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/error/errno\">errno</a></span> may be set.\n</p><p>As all functions from Dynamic Memory TR, <code>strdup</code> is only guaranteed to be available if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_ALLOC_LIB__</span></code> is defined by the implementation and if the user defines <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">__STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT2__</span></code> to the integer constant <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span></span></code> before including <code>string.h</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  str1\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  pointer to the null-terminated byte string to duplicate\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A pointer to the newly allocated string, or a null pointer if an error occurred.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The function is identical to the  <a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/strdup.html\" data-external=\"1\">POSIX strdup</a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#ifdef __STDC_ALLOC_LIB__</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#define __STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT2__ 1</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#else</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200809L</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#endif</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>s1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"String\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>s2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> strdup<span class=\"br0\">(</span>s1<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw407\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strcmp\"><span class=\"kw559\">strcmp</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s1, s2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/memory/free\"><span class=\"kw406\">free</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/experimental/dynamic/strndup\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strndup</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-dynamic-tr t-mark-ts\">(dynamic memory TR)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   allocate a copy of a string up to specified size <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strcpy\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strcpy</span><span>strcpy_s</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(C11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   copies one string to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/memory/malloc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>malloc</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   allocates memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C features"},{"path":"experimental/dynamic","title":"Dynamic memory extensions"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"strdup","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Returns a pointer to a null-terminated byte string, which is a duplicate of the string pointed to by str1."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"str1"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A pointer to the newly allocated string, or a null pointer if an error occurred."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The function is identical to the POSIX strdup."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"strndup","note":"allocate a copy of a string up to specified size"},{"label":"strcpy, strcpy_s","note":"copies one string to another"},{"label":"malloc","note":"allocates memory"}]}]},"standards":["C11"],"wordCount":194,"codeBlockCount":1}
